|~ `::null`, the kind of null, and what is declared under it: the
   refusal of a payload of another kind, and its text and its keyword.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:null
  |~~ Null is the absence of a value, the one value of its kind. It
      stands where a part is missing: `query` reads a part softly and
      answers null where there is none, `{:name "Ann"} | query /age`
      answering `null`, a JSON `null` reads as it, and `coalesce` answers
      a fallback for it, `{:name "Ann"} | query /age | coalesce 0`
      answering `0`.

      It is written `null`, and `::null#null` is the same value. It
      ranks first in the one order, before every boolean, and JSON
      writes it as `null`. `get /age` reads strictly: a missing part is a
      failure there, never null, so a misspelled field is
      found where it is read.
      ::snippet~(::null | manifest) lists its verbs.
      ::link~(::any/coalesce) ::link~(::path)
      ::link~(::qlang/values)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ Null, read as itself. ~~| ::null
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::null` reads its payload as null; a payload of another kind
            is refused.
        ~~|
    | proves :isNull |~~ Null is of `::null`. ~~| ~(null | tag | eq ::null)
    | proves :buildsNull
        |~~ Null under its own tag is null. ~~|
        ~(::null#null | eq null)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(::null#1 !| get [tag (found | tag)]
          | eq [::null/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::number]);

:null/toKeyword
  |~~ Answers `:null`, the key `groupBy` files an absent field under,
      `groupBy (query /country)`.
      ::link~(::vec/groupBy) ::link~(::any/coalesce)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ `:null`. ~~| ::keyword
    | proves :readsTheKeyGroupByFiledItUnder
        |~~ Null turns into the key `groupBy` files an absent field under.
        ~~|
        ~([{:country "US"} {}] | groupBy (query /country)
          | at (null | toKeyword) | eq [{}])
    | impl ::builtin{};

:null/toString
  |~~ Answers `"null"`, the text `print` and `json` write for null, as
      every atom answers the text of its literal; a field that may be
      absent is given a text of its own by `coalesce`.
      ::link~(::null/toKeyword) ::link~(::any/coalesce)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ `"null"`. ~~| ::string
    | proves :writesTheLiteral
        |~~ Null turns into the text of its literal. ~~|
        ~(null | toString | eq "null")
    | impl ~("null");

